From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 10:46:57 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: msm8998-google-wahoo: enable IPA

Enable the IPA block so the modem gets a data path, and have the AP load
the GSI firmware rather than the modem.

With the modem as GSI loader it is supposed to initialise GSI and raise
the "ipa-setup-ready" smp2p interrupt; on wahoo that interrupt never
arrives, so ipa_qmi_ready() never fires, ipa_modem_start() is never
called, and the rmnet netdev is never created. The vendor ships
qcom/msm8998/wahoo/ipa_fws.mbn, whose ELF program headers are based at
paddr 0 spanning 0x7000 - fully relocatable - so qcom_mdt_load places it
wherever memory-region points, and the existing ipa_fw_mem carveout
(0x10000 at 0x95200000) is untouched by this board's memory map.

msm8998-oneplus-common.dtsi already loads GSI firmware from the AP on
this SoC.

Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 .../boot/dts/qcom/msm8998-google-wahoo.dtsi   | 34 +++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 23 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998-google-wahoo.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998-google-wahoo.dtsi
index be6edb5d0c36..4c118b66ed31 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998-google-wahoo.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998-google-wahoo.dtsi
@@ -596,17 +596,29 @@ &ufsphy {
 	vddp-ref-clk-always-on;
 };
 
-/*
- * milestone-2 TODO (ipa, explicitly out of milestone-1 scope): our &ipa
- * override (GSI firmware load, memory-region, "okay" status -- see
- * taimen-v6.0's msm8998-google-wahoo.dtsi for the full node with modem
- * WLAN-datapath rationale) has no base node to attach to: 6.18's
- * msm8998.dtsi carries no top-level "ipa" node at all yet, unlike our
- * 6.0 base. Needs the ipa SoC node ported into msm8998.dtsi first
- * (the drivers/net/ipa code is also unported -- gsi.c, ipa_gsi.c,
- * ipa_modem.c are all in the milestone-2 list), then this override can
- * come back.
- */
+&ipa {
+	status = "okay";
+
+	/*
+	 * The AP loads the GSI firmware here, as msm8998-oneplus-common.dtsi
+	 * already does on this SoC -- NOT "modem". With the modem as loader
+	 * it is supposed to initialise GSI and raise the "ipa-setup-ready"
+	 * smp2p interrupt; on wahoo that interrupt never arrives, so
+	 * ipa_qmi_ready() never fires, ipa_modem_start() is never called and
+	 * the rmnet netdev is never created. Without that netdev nothing
+	 * matches ModemManager's 77-mm-qcom-soc.rules (SUBSYSTEM=="net",
+	 * DRIVERS=="ipa"), so no modem object is ever exposed.
+	 *
+	 * The vendor ships qcom/msm8998/wahoo/ipa_fws.mbn, and its ELF program
+	 * headers are based at paddr 0 spanning 0x7000, i.e. fully relocatable,
+	 * so qcom_mdt_load places it wherever memory-region points. ipa_fw_mem
+	 * is 0x10000 at 0x95200000 and /proc/iomem confirms 95200000-95214fff
+	 * is reserved and otherwise unused on this device.
+	 */
+	qcom,gsi-loader = "self";
+	memory-region = <&ipa_fw_mem>;
+	firmware-name = "qcom/msm8998/wahoo/ipa_fws.mbn";
+};
 
 &wifi {
 	status = "okay";
